    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0293" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v11/pg267"/>

                <head>104. Letter From the Assistant Secretary of State for International
                    Organization Affairs (Key)
                    to the Representative at the United Nations (Lodge)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d104-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1955-04-01">April 1, 1955</date>.</hi></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Cabot</hi>: Thank you for the copy of your letter to the
                    Secretary on the UN membership problem.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d104-f2"/></p>
                <p>I think that you may be interested in the enclosed preliminary draft of a
                    memorandum on membership on which we have been working here for some time. It
                    has not been shown to anyone outside our Bureau and of course has not been seen
                    by the Secretary. Your comments would be very helpful to us. As you will see,
                        <pb facs="0294" n="268" xml:id="pg268"/> we also are inclined to feel that
                    we should follow up our non-member participation proposal. Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">David McK.
                                Key</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d104-f3"
                    /></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d104-a1.xml" xpointer="d104-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d104-a2.xml" xpointer="d104-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
